//ERR 12 3 12 6
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// `1 == 1` is always true, but it is an expression, not the literal `true`, and
// the exemption in 29_while_true_returns_from_inside.cpl is syntactic: a
// condition that merely happens to always hold is still assumed to fall
// through. Constant-folding conditions to decide reachability would put the
// compiler in the business of proving termination.
//
// So this has to be rejected, and written with a `ret` after the loop instead —
// exactly as 28_a_loop_followed_by_a_return.cpl is.

fn f n
    while 1 == 1
        if n > 0
            ret 1
        n++

fn main
    out "{f(-3)}"
